With the next Referral Season, we’re making a change to the way referrals work in Albion Online. From October 1, 2025, only Premium time purchased with real money from the Albion Online Web Shop or ingame store will count towards referral rewards (30 days of Premium or more). This means that Premium purchased with Gold or Silver will no longer earn rewards for the referrer. In making this change, our aim is to encourage organic referrals, while we also hope to see a downward effect on Gold prices as a result of this and will be observing developments there.

If you have any questions or feedback about these changes, you can visit this dedicated forum thread. For more on Referral Seasons, and to find your referral link, see this page (login required).

//assets.albiononline.com/uploads/media/default/media/a223dfd54182c21ade978aec1a41480233a668a7.jpeg

As the current Guild Season reaches its climax, it’s already time to get ready for Albion’s next major content update. On April 15, Foundations will launch, bringing with it a host of new developments and improvements. Fortifications are upgradable defensive features for territories, and Siege Banners offer possibilities for attackers and defenders alike. Territory Activity Chests offer enticing rewards for territory owners - as well as their rivals. New Crystal Weapons are coming, with a range of powerful spells. And a Spectator Mode allows Albion’s creators to broadcast Arena battles and tournaments. With all this and more, Foundations opens the gates to new forms of warfare in Albion.

//assets.albiononline.com/uploads/media/default/media/451d5ca1489731a7a73517cf3ae7ef7e7e6c4bcb.jpeg
Raise the Banner
Fortifications offer formidable defensive structures for guilds of all sizes, and will bring forth new tactics and strategies in territorial combat. These structures, and their guards, can be further upgraded by guilds who invest the time and resources, becoming mighty barriers against those who seek to raid and conquer. In addition, Siege Banners complement this, adding a new twist to territory fights by providing opportunities for attacking and defending guilds alike.

//assets.albiononline.com/uploads/media/default/media/e5b8e2e96e69701d179d3e0cdefb828cd6f88e5e.jpeg
Territories Transformed
Territory Activity Chests encourage constant activity around territories - but the more value they accrue, the more enticing they become to potential attackers. Territories in the Outlands also now have new layouts. Meanwhile, Prime Times have been adjusted across the different servers, to provide more consistent action for each region.

//assets.albiononline.com/uploads/media/default/media/a1df58574894e6b882cda6507728b7bd34fb8c2c.jpeg
Let Battle Commence
New Crystal Weapons are coming, offering an array of powerful and prestigious prizes to top season performers. Hammers are getting fresh and formidable new spells too, shaking up the combat meta. And a new Spectator Mode gives creators the freedom to set up and broadcast their own Arena battles, opening the door to exciting, player-run tournaments.

With all this, Foundations lays the groundwork for some exciting new developments to warfare in Albion. For more details, check out the official update page:

LEARN MORE

